# LOCKED RULE — visible browser + unbreakable one-browser session

This is locked. Do not interpret, weaken, or skip it.

QAFusionX is a sequential pipeline. That does **not** mean crawl or GUI tests run silently "inside the pipeline".

When **any user** runs QAFusionX on **their device**:

1. Open a **separate real browser window on that device** (headed Chromium / Chrome / Edge). The work happens in that window.
2. The user watches every navigation, popup, and click.
3. **Never** run crawl or GUI tests as a silent/headless/background pipeline job. No hidden webview. No API-only substitute for a GUI pass.
4. If this machine has no display, stop and tell the user to run QAFusionX on their own computer so the browser can open there. Do not continue headless.
5. API tests may run without a window. Round 1, Round 2, and GUI scripts may not.

## UNBREAKABLE SESSION (mandatory)

6. **One browser only.** Open once at the start of GUI work. Keep it open for Round 1 → Round 2 → all stories → maker → checker → suite.
7. **Never close mid-flow.** Do not close between stories, screens, rounds, or maker→checker. Do not open a second Chromium "for the next story".
8. Logout/login (maker → checker) stays **inside the same window**.
9. `closeBrowser` is **end-of-flow only** (workflow reset or user ends the full QA run).
10. Engine must **reuse** the live page (`openVisibleBrowser` / `getPage`); `openTarget` loads the **entry URL once only**.
11. **MOUSE-CLICK-ONLY (LOCKED):** after that single entry load, never `page.goto`, never type another URL, never deep-link. Advance Round 1/2 / stories / maker→checker **only by mouse clicks**.

`QAFUSIONX_HEADED=0` is rejected by the engine. There is no silent mode.

Sinhala: එක browser එකක් open කරලා digatama යන්න. URL එකක් වරක්. ඊට පස්සේ mouse click විතරක්. අතරේ close / URL reload තහනම්.
